msgid "Conditional extension dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus extension dependencies are usually configured in the same way as any "
"other project dependencies in a project's build file, for example the Maven "
"`pom.xml` or the Gradle build scripts. However, Quarkus also supports types "
"of dependencies that aren't supported out-of-the-box by Maven and Gradle. "
"Conditional Quarkus extension dependencies is one such example."
msgstr ""

msgid "Conditional Dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A conditional dependency is a dependency that is activated only if a certain "
"condition is satisfied. If the condition is not satisfied then the "
"dependency **will not** be activated. In that regard, conditional "
"dependencies can be categorized as optional, meaning they may or may not "
"appear in the resulting dependency graph."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A typical example of a conditional dependency would be a component that "
"should be added to the classpath **only** in case all of its required "
"dependencies are present on the classpath. If one or more of the component's "
"required dependencies aren't available, instead of failing, the component "
"should simply not be added."
msgstr ""

msgid "Conditional Quarkus Extension Dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A Quarkus extension may declare one or more conditional dependencies on "
"other Quarkus extensions or regular Maven artifacts."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Let's consider the following scenario as an example: `quarkus-extension-a` "
"has an optional dependency on `quarkus-extension-b` which should be included "
"in a Quarkus application only if `quarkus-extension-c` is found among the "
"application dependencies (direct or transitive). In this case, the presence "
"of `quarkus-extension-c` is the condition, which, if satisfied, will trigger "
"inclusion of the `quarkus-extension-b` when Quarkus application dependencies "
"are resolved."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The condition which triggers activation of an extension is configured in the "
"extension's `META-INF/quarkus-extension.properties`, which is included in "
"the runtime artifact of the extension. Extension developers can add the "
"following configuration to express the condition which would have to be "
"satisfied for the extension to be activated:"
msgstr ""

msgid "runtime Quarkus extension artifact ID;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the goal that generates the extension descriptor which every Quarkus runtime "
"extension project should be configured with;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"configuration of the dependency condition which will have to be satisfied "
"for this extension to be added to a Quarkus application expressed as a list "
"of artifacts that must be present among the application dependencies;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"an artifact key (in the format of `groupId:artifactId[:<classifier>:"
"<extension>]` but typically simply `<groupId>:<artifactId>`) of the artifact "
"that must be present among the application dependencies for the condition to "
"be satisfied."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `dependencyCondition` element may contain more than `artifact`, in which "
"case all the configured artifacts must be present on the classpath for the "
"condition to be satisfied."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now, having a dependency condition recorded in the descriptor of the "
"`quarkus-extension-b`, other extensions may declare a conditional dependency "
"on it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A conditional dependency is configured in the runtime artifact of a Quarkus "
"extension. In this example, the `quarkus-extension-a` will declare a "
"conditional dependency on the `quarkus-extension-b`, which can be done in "
"the following two ways."
msgstr ""

msgid "Declaring a dependency as <code>optional</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If an extension includes a dependency condition in its descriptor, other "
"extensions may configure a conditional dependency on it by simply adding "
"`<optional>true</optional>` to the dependency configuration. In our example "
"it would look like this:"
msgstr ""

msgid "the runtime extension artifact `quarkus-extension-a`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"declares an optional Maven dependency on the runtime extension artifact "
"`quarkus-extension-b`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Given that `quarkus-extension-b` includes a dependency condition, Quarkus "
"will interpret an optional dependency on the `quarkus-extension-b` as "
"conditional."
msgstr ""

msgid "the deployment extension artifact `quarkus-extension-a-deployment`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"declares an optional Maven dependency on the deployment extension artifact "
"`quarkus-extension-b-deployment`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Declaring a conditional dependency in the Quarkus extension descriptor"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Conditional dependencies can also be configured in the Quarkus extension "
"descriptor directly. Here is an example of how it can be done in the Quarkus "
"extension plugin configuration of the `quarkus-extension-a`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "the runtime Quarkus extension artifact ID;"
msgstr ""

msgid "the conditional dependency configuration element;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the artifact coordinates of conditional dependencies on other extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this case, the Maven dependency is not at all required in the `pom.xml` "
"file."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev mode-only extension dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extensions can also declare conditional dependencies on other extensions "
"using dev mode as the condition or one of the conditions for those "
"dependencies to be activated."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Dev mode-only extension dependencies can be configured in the Quarkus "
"extension plugin in the following way:"
msgstr ""

msgid "conditional dependencies that should be evaluated only in dev mode;"
msgstr ""

msgid "the artifact coordinates of a conditional dependency."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus-extension-b`, in this example, may or may not define its own "
"condition to be evaluated."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the `quarkus-extension-b` does not define a dependency condition on its "
"own (there is no dependency condition recorded in its `META-INF/quarkus-"
"extension.properties`), the `quarkus-extension-b` will only be added as a "
"dependency of the `quarkus-extension-a` in dev mode but not in other modes "
"(prod or test)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the `quarkus-extension-b` does define a dependency condition on its own "
"(a dependency condition recorded in its `META-INF/quarkus-extension."
"properties`), the `quarkus-extension-b` will be added as a dependency of the "
"`quarkus-extension-a` in dev mode only if its condition is satisfied (the "
"artifacts it requires are present in the application dependency graph)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dev mode dependencies on regular Maven artifacts"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extensions may also declare conditional dependencies on regular Maven "
"artifacts, that are not Quarkus extensions. Given that regular Maven "
"artifacts do not include Quarkus metadata, the condition for their inclusion "
"is configured by an extension depending on them."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In this example `library-b` is a regular Maven artifact that will be added "
"as a dependency of the `quarkus-extension-a` only when an application is "
"launched in dev mode."
msgstr ""
